## Hard rules
- NEVER edit `.unity`, `.prefab`, `.asset` or `.meta` files directly. If wiring is needed, write an Editor script or list the manual Editor steps for me.
- For every new `[SerializeField]`, tell me what to assign in the Inspector.
- No `FindObjectOfType` in Update loops; cache references. Avoid allocations in Update (no LINQ, no string building per frame).
- Dev builds use Google's test ad unit IDs only. Real IDs are set via the release config.
- Don't add packages without stating why.

## Commands (Mac)
- Unity: `"/Applications/Unity/Hub/Editor/<ver>/Unity.app/Contents/MacOS/Unity"`
- EditMode tests: `<Unity> -batchmode -nographics -projectPath . -runTests -testPlatform EditMode -testResults results.xml -logFile -`
- Android .aab: `<Unity> -batchmode -quit -projectPath . -executeMethod BuildScript.BuildAndroid -logFile -`
- If the Editor has the project open, batchmode can't run — ask me to close it or I'll run tests in the Editor.

## Definition of done
1. Acceptance criteria met. 2. Compiles with no errors or new warnings. 3. EditMode tests for new logic pass. 4. Manual Editor steps listed. 5. `docs/TASKS.md` updated. 6. Reply in ≤ 5 lines.

## Token discipline
Read only files the task names. Never read Library/ or large asset files. Show only relevant log lines.
